id: pm-github-mes8
title: Packed projection fixture cleanup can mask its own test outcome
description: "Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-github#202 (filed 2026-10-30, missed by the blind issue watch). test/import-projection.test.ts on current main still ends with a bare 'finally { rmSync(base, { recursive: true, force: true }) }' (line ~258), so an ENOTEMPTY from the isolated HOME teardown replaces an earlier exception from the protected body and the receipt proves neither that the packed import assertions passed nor that they failed. Observed once on the merged CodeQL-pin PR #200 head (Node 22, run 41029600935). Make the final cleanup non-fatal (or run it outside the assertion path and log residuals), so a teardown race cannot mask the actual test outcome; keep the two Bun lanes green."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: changelog-unreleased,ci,fixtures,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#202"
created_at: "2026-11-02T09:17:17.491Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T13:59:55.662Z"
author: pi-glm
resolution: Fixture-local global storage and supported inline flush make producer completion precede teardown. Bounded removal preserves the original thrown value on success and reports both failures through AggregateError when cleanup also fails. All original packed consumer assertions and deadlines remain intact.
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T12:43:01.308Z",codex-astra,Read #202 in full. Main 03c3059 retains bare finally removal in the packed projection fixture. Investigate the pinned CLI producer lifecycle and add failing real-process regressions before repair. Preserve primary plus cleanup errors and every mixed import JSON/TOON npm/Bun assertion and deadline. No SDK mocks or live provider data.
  "2026-11-06T12:46:19.553Z",codex-astra,"Failing-first evidence: the extracted original lifecycle fails 3 of 5 regressions: inherited global storage escapes the fixture, the actual pinned CLI exits before its delayed loopback telemetry delivery finishes, and a real child-created EACCES replaces the primary error. Two positive controls pass. The SDK runtime spawns an unreferenced detached telemetry-flush child unless PM_TELEMETRY_INLINE_FLUSH is set. Repair applies that supported lifecycle flag and fixture-local PM_GLOBAL_PATH, plus bounded removal retries and AggregateError with original cause. The unchanged baseline packed consumer separately timed out in installation; no import outcome is inferred."
  "2026-11-06T12:55:55.986Z",codex-astra,"Verification: new lifecycle tests pass 5/5 under Node and native Bun (zero skips), including a passing pm test --run --progress --only-index 1 receipt. Lint, production typecheck and test typecheck pass. Disposable behavioral reverts fail independently: remove inline flush 0/1; remove global isolation 0/1; restore bare cleanup 1/2 with the primary-preservation case failing. The final cleanup function was reverted again after lint-driven restructuring and still fails. Fixed rerun passes 5/5. The original packed fixture and two repaired attempts time out in package installation before import assertions; unchanged deadlines are retained and this separate local limit is tracked by pm-github-r14n. Hosted final-head CI and bot review remain pending before publication."
  "2026-11-06T13:03:27.820Z",codex-astra,"Final self-review found that separate cleanup success controls passed the original helper, while the task requires each new test to fail on behavioral revert. Grouped those controls with primary-error preservation into one regression without removing assertions or changing deadlines. The final file now has three regression tests; each must fail on its relevant function revert. Revalidating before the next push and review queue renewal."
  "2026-11-06T13:06:23.564Z",codex-astra,"Final grouped regressions pass 3/3 under Node, native Bun and pm test --run --progress --only-index 1, with zero skips. Each new test now fails its relevant behavioral revert independently (0/1 for inline producer lifecycle, global-root isolation and primary-error preservation). The underlying success and cleanup-only failure controls are retained in the same regression. Lint and both typechecks pass again. This supersedes the earlier five-test layout only; the implementation, original packed assertions, child deadline, fixture timeout and coverage thresholds are unchanged. PR #223 is open; refresh CodeRabbit and CI evidence on the next pushed head."
  "2026-11-06T13:49:36.149Z",codex-astra,"CodeRabbit round 1 completed on c302e5d with two valid findings: the native Bun test still launches Node via nodeToolingExecutable, and chmod cannot force EACCES for a privileged runner. Add a real child-runtime receipt that fails when Bun is replaced by Node; run the producer with process.execPath. Replace permission-dependent failure setup with an explicit cleanup fault seam while keeping actual SDK trackers, OS children, default real removal controls and the real delayed-producer regression. No SDK mocks, skipped cases, deadline increases or gate changes."
  "2026-11-06T13:57:20.332Z",codex-astra,"Round 1 fixes verified locally: the real preload receipt first failed under Bun because the producer reported Node; process.execPath now executes the active runtime. The permission-dependent failure control is replaced by a typed injectable remover, with real default-removal success controls, real SDK tracker setup and a real child-completion marker. New Node and native Bun suites pass 3/3, zero skips. Runtime-selection revert fails the full Bun file 2 pass / 1 fail / 0 skips; reverting aggregation while retaining the fault seam fails the selected cleanup regression 0/1. Inline-flush and global-root reverts also still fail 0/1 on the revised tests. Lint and both typechecks pass. The linked full projection rerun remains in progress at unchanged deadlines."
  "2026-11-06T13:59:51.173Z",codex-astra,"The complete linked projection rerun now passes: lifecycle 3/3 and import-projection 6/6, zero failures/cancellations/skips. This includes the original packed npm/native Bun JSON/TOON mixed-import byte/history and preview assertions at the unchanged 45-second child and 600-second packed-test deadlines. The earlier installation timeouts remain recorded in pm-github-r14n; the latest run establishes focused local acceptance without a deadline increase. Round 1 fixes will be pushed together, replied to in one batch, and queued for a fresh current-head review/CI."
